  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0050-p00050",
      "source_en": "A flash of color flew up into the tree. “Look, an oriole!” someone said. With the tip of its tail cocked, it made no sound, its brilliant strangeness lit up the dense green, like spring light, like flame, like passion. Waiting for it to sing, we watched in stillness, afraid we might startle it. But as soon as it spread its wings, it burst through the dense foliage and became a colored cloud; It flew away, vanished, was gone, like spring light, like flame, like passion. Written in early 1930",
